  "note": "Election of 15 members of Banbridge Urban District Council on 15 May 1936; only eleven candidates were nominated, five retiring members being deemed re-elected, so there was no contest. No poll. Coburn and Boyd were deemed re-elected after a ballot by the returning officer for the two remaining seats. Baxter was the only new member. Returned unopposed."
